<article class="om-k" id="omegamaxxing-kitchen" aria-label="Omegamaxxing in the kitchen">

  {%- comment -%} ============================ 05 COOKING ============================ {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign img_wide = images['omegamaxxing-03-sliced-salmon-garden.jpg'] -%}
  <section class="om-band" id="om-cook">
    <div class="page-width om-stack" style="gap: var(--sp-8);">
      <div class="om-split" style="align-items: start;">
        <div class="om-head" data-om-animate>
          <p class="{{ kicker_class }} om-label">Chapter 5 · Cooking to protect omega-3s</p>
          <h2 class="heading title-xl tracking-heading leading-none">Reduce heat, air and time.</h2>
          <p class="text-lg leading-normal">EPA and DHA are fragile. Their structure has several weak points that break down with heat and oxygen, a process called oxidation. The more heat, air and time, the more omega-3 you lose.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="om-stack">
          <p class="{{ kicker_class }} om-label">Cooking methods ranked</p>
          <div class="om-grid om-grid--2">
            <div class="om-num om-rank" data-om-animate><span class="om-rank__word">Best</span><h3 class="heading title-sm leading-tight">Poach, steam, sous vide</h3><p class="text-base leading-normal">Low, controlled heat (usually under 200°F) and little contact with air. The gentlest option.</p></div>
            <div class="om-num om-rank" data-om-animate data-om-delay="80"><span class="om-rank__word">Good</span><h3 class="heading title-sm leading-tight">Bake or roast at 275–325°F</h3><p class="text-base leading-normal">Short cook time; pull before it’s opaque all the way through. Wrapping in foil or parchment (en papillote) keeps air out.</p></div>
            <div class="om-num om-rank" data-om-animate data-om-delay="160"><span class="om-rank__word">Okay</span><h3 class="heading title-sm leading-tight">Quick sear, grill, air fry</h3><p class="text-base leading-normal">High heat but brief. Sear hot and fast, skin-side down first so the skin shields the flesh.</p></div>
            <div class="om-num om-rank" data-om-animate data-om-delay="240"><span class="om-rank__word">Minimize</span><h3 class="heading title-sm leading-tight">Deep frying, long pan frying</h3><p class="text-base leading-normal">High heat plus hot oil and air does the most damage to omega-3s.</p></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <figure class="om-media om-media--wide">
        <media-element class="block w-full h-full" data-parallax="0.15" data-parallax-dir="vertical">
          <picture class="block w-full h-full" is="animate-picture" data-animate="zoom-out">
            {%- if img_wide != blank -%}{{ img_wide | image_url: width: 2400 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', sizes: '100vw', widths: '800,1200,1600,2000,2400', alt: 'A platter of sliced salmon on a garden table.' }}{%- endif -%}
          </picture>
        </media-element>
        <ul class="om-chips om-chips--over" role="list" data-om-fly>
          <li><span class="om-chip">{{ om_check }}gentlest: poach, steam, sous vide</span></li>
        </ul>
      </figure>

      <div class="om-head" data-om-animate>
        <p class="{{ kicker_class }} om-label">Chapter 5 · Cooking to protect omega-3s</p>
        <h3 class="heading title-lg tracking-heading leading-tight">Practical rules</h3>
      </div>
      {%- capture om_rules -%}omegamaxxing-22-thermometer-check.jpg|A thermometer checking a tray of baked salmon fillets.|Cook to medium, not well-done.|Pull salmon or steelhead at 120–130°F inside; it will rise to about 135°F as it rests. Every extra minute of heat means more oxidation.^omegamaxxing-21-lemon-squeeze-bake.jpg|Lemon squeezed over salmon on a sheet pan.|Favor moist methods.|Poaching in broth or olive oil, steaming and en papillote baking all limit air exposure.^omegamaxxing-23-oven-bake.jpg|A tray of salmon going into the oven.|Reheat gently, or not at all.|Warm leftovers in a low oven or steamer, or eat them cold in a salad or poke bowl. Avoid microwaving on high or re-searing.^omegamaxxing-16-sashimi-plate.jpg|Sashimi slices on a ceramic plate.|Raw and lightly cured keep the most.|Sashimi, poke, crudo and ceviche skip heat entirely, so you get the full omega-3 content of a sashimi-grade portion.{%- endcapture -%}
      {%- assign rules = om_rules | split: '^' -%}
      <div class="om-grid om-grid--4">
        {%- for row in rules -%}
          {%- assign r = row | split: '|' -%}
          {%- assign rimg = images[r[0]] -%}
          <div class="om-rule" data-om-animate data-om-delay="{{ forloop.index0 | times: 80 }}">
            <div class="om-media om-media--square">
              {%- if rimg != blank -%}{{ rimg | image_url: width: 900 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 22vw, (min-width: 600px) 45vw, 100vw', widths: '400,600,900', alt: r[1] }}{%- endif -%}
            </div>
            <h4 class="heading title-sm leading-tight">{{ r[2] }}</h4>
            <p class="text-base leading-normal">{{ r[3] }}</p>
          </div>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
      <div class="om-notes">
        <div>
          <p class="{{ kicker_class }} om-label">Takeaway</p>
          <p class="text-lg leading-snug">Low heat, less air, less time. Raw or gently cooked fish keeps the most omega-3s.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="{{ kicker_class }} om-label">Raw and undercooked</p>
          {%- comment -%} Verbatim: claims guide §9.5. {%- endcomment -%}
          <p class="text-lg leading-snug">Eating raw or undercooked seafood may increase your risk of foodborne illness. The FDA conservatively suggests cooking to an internal temperature of 145°F.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="{{ kicker_class }} om-label">Pregnant?</p>
          <p class="text-lg leading-snug">Cook fish to 145°F. Poaching, steaming and en papillote cook fish all the way through gently. More in <a class="link" href="#om-pregnancy">pregnancy and breastfeeding</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} ============================ 06 ABSORBING ============================ {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign img_abs = images['omegamaxxing-08-eggs-roe-handheld.jpg'] -%}
  {%- assign img_de = images['omegamaxxing-06-greens-avocado-nuts.jpg'] -%}
  <section class="om-band om-tone--sage" id="om-absorb">
    <div class="page-width om-stack" style="gap: var(--sp-8);">
      <div class="om-split om-split--flip">
        <div class="om-stack">
          <div class="om-head" data-om-animate>
            <p class="{{ kicker_class }} om-label">Chapter 6</p>
            <h2 class="heading title-xl tracking-heading leading-none">Absorbing and using omega-3s</h2>
          </div>
          <p class="text-lg leading-normal">Getting EPA and DHA onto your plate is only half the job. Omega-3s are fat-soluble, so what you eat them with changes how much your body takes in and keeps.</p>
          <p class="{{ kicker_class }} om-label" style="margin-block-start: var(--sp-4);">Four habits that help</p>
          <div class="om-grid om-grid--2">
            <div class="om-num" data-om-animate><span class="text-sm text-opacity">01</span><h3 class="heading title-sm leading-tight">Eat them with fat.</h3><p class="text-base leading-normal">Your body needs bile to absorb omega-3s, and bile is released when you eat fat. A drizzle of olive oil, some avocado, or the fish’s own skin-on fat is enough.</p></div>
            <div class="om-num" data-om-animate data-om-delay="80"><span class="text-sm text-opacity">02</span><h3 class="heading title-sm leading-tight">Pair them with vitamin E.</h3><p class="text-base leading-normal">Vitamin E sits beside omega-3s in your cell membranes and protects them from oxidation.</p></div>
            <div class="om-num" data-om-animate data-om-delay="160"><span class="text-sm text-opacity">03</span><h3 class="heading title-sm leading-tight">Keep vitamin D in the mix.</h3><p class="text-base leading-normal">Vitamin D is another nutrient fatty fish supplies. We test and publish omega-3, protein, selenium, vitamin D and B12.</p></div>
            <div class="om-num" data-om-animate data-om-delay="240"><span class="text-sm text-opacity">04</span><h3 class="heading title-sm leading-tight">Watch your omega-6s.</h3><p class="text-base leading-normal">Omega-3 and omega-6 fats compete for the same spots in your cell membranes and the same enzymes. Fewer seed oils means more room for omega-3s to work (see <a class="link" href="#om-labels">Chapter 3</a>).</p></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="om-split__media om-stack">
          <div class="om-media om-media--tall">
            {%- if img_abs != blank -%}{{ img_abs | image_url: width: 1333 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 45vw, 100vw', widths: '500,800,1100,1333', alt: 'A plate of eggs, salmon roe and avocado held in one hand.' }}{%- endif -%}
            <ul class="om-chips om-chips--over om-chips--top" role="list" data-om-fly>
              <li style="--om-delay: 0ms;"><span class="om-chip">{{ om_check }}with fat</span></li>
              <li style="--om-delay: 140ms;"><span class="om-chip">{{ om_check }}with vitamin E</span></li>
              <li style="--om-delay: 280ms;"><span class="om-chip">{{ om_check }}with fewer seed oils</span></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="om-card">
            <p class="{{ kicker_class }} om-label">Whole food vs. supplements</p>
            {%- comment -%} Verbatim: claims guide §4.E, with its rider that supplements work. {%- endcomment -%}
            <p class="heading title-sm leading-tight om-italic">A capsule gives you two molecules. A fillet gives you the whole matrix.</p>
            <p class="text-base leading-normal">Supplements can have a useful place, including for people who don’t eat seafood or have specific nutritional needs.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="om-split">
        <div class="om-stack">
          <div class="om-head" data-om-animate>
            <p class="{{ kicker_class }} om-label">Chapter 6 · Absorbing and using omega-3s</p>
            <h3 class="heading title-lg tracking-heading leading-tight">Vitamin D and vitamin E sources</h3>
          </div>
          <div class="om-grid om-grid--2">
            <div class="om-stack" style="gap: var(--sp-3);">
              <h4 class="title-sm leading-tight" style="font-family: var(--font-body-family); font-weight: 600;">Vitamin D sources</h4>
              <ul class="om-list text-lg leading-snug" role="list">
                <li>Fatty fish like salmon, trout, mackerel, sardines and herring (the same fish that are high in omega-3s)</li>
                <li>Egg yolks</li>
                <li>Beef liver</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="om-stack" style="gap: var(--sp-3);">
              <h4 class="title-sm leading-tight" style="font-family: var(--font-body-family); font-weight: 600;">Vitamin E sources</h4>
              <ul class="om-list text-lg leading-snug" role="list">
                <li>Sunflower seeds</li>
                <li>Almonds and hazelnuts</li>
                <li>Peanuts and peanut butter</li>
                <li>Avocado</li>
                <li>Spinach and Swiss chard</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="om-card">
            <p class="{{ kicker_class }} om-label">Pregnant?</p>
            <p class="text-base leading-normal om-italic">Beef liver is very high in preformed vitamin A. Ask your OB about liver and vitamin A during pregnancy.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="om-media om-media--land">
          {%- if img_de != blank -%}{{ img_de | image_url: width: 1800 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 45vw, 100vw', widths: '500,800,1200,1800', alt: 'Chard, spinach, avocado, almonds and seeds on a round wooden board.' }}{%- endif -%}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} ============================ 07 TOGETHER ============================ {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign img_tog = images['omegamaxxing-15-crudo-platter-overhead.jpg'] -%}
  {%- assign img_cut = images['omegamaxxing-12-slicing-salmon.jpg'] -%}
  <section class="om-band" id="om-together">
    <div class="page-width om-stack" style="gap: var(--sp-8);">
      <div class="om-split" style="align-items: center;">
        <div class="om-stack">
          <div class="om-head" data-om-animate>
            <p class="{{ kicker_class }} om-label">Chapter 7</p>
            <h2 class="heading title-xl tracking-heading leading-none">Putting it all together</h2>
          </div>
          <p class="{{ kicker_class }} om-label" style="margin-block-start: var(--sp-6);">A weekly target</p>
          <p class="om-big" data-om-animate>2–3</p>
          <p class="heading title-sm leading-tight om-italic">servings a week, from the FDA/EPA Best Choices list.</p>
          <p class="text-lg leading-normal">Start with FDA/EPA’s 2–3 servings a week, test your Omega-3 Index, and adjust from there.</p>
        </div>
        <media-element class="om-media om-media--tall block" data-parallax="0.12" data-parallax-dir="vertical">
          <picture class="block w-full h-full" is="animate-picture" data-animate="zoom-out">
            {%- if img_tog != blank -%}{{ img_tog | image_url: width: 1600 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 45vw, 100vw', widths: '500,800,1200,1600', alt: 'Salmon crudo on a platter, seen from above.' }}{%- endif -%}
          </picture>
        </media-element>
      </div>

      <div class="om-head" data-om-animate>
        <p class="{{ kicker_class }} om-label">Chapter 7 · Putting it all together</p>
        <h3 class="heading title-lg tracking-heading leading-tight">Quick checklist</h3>
      </div>
      <ul class="om-checks text-lg leading-snug" role="list">
        <li>Test your Omega-3 Index and omega-6:omega-3 ratio, then retest after 3–4 months.</li>
        <li>Buy fattier, cold-water fish first (salmon, steelhead).</li>
        <li>Cut back on refined seed oils and processed foods.</li>
        <li>Keep portions frozen until the day you cook them; thaw overnight in the fridge.</li>
        <li>Default to poaching, steaming, low-temp baking or a quick sear.</li>
        <li>Cook to rare or medium, not well-done — pull it a little earlier than you think.</li>
        <li>Eat it with fat and vitamin E: olive oil, avocado, nuts or seeds.</li>
        <li>Try a raw preparation (sashimi, poke, crudo) now and then: nothing is lost to cooking.</li>
        <li>If you supplement, choose a fresh, third-party-tested product and take it with a meal.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="om-media om-media--wide">
        {%- if img_cut != blank -%}{{ img_cut | image_url: width: 2400 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', sizes: '100vw', widths: '800,1200,1600,2000,2400', alt: 'Cubing a salmon fillet on a dark cutting board.' }}{%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%}
    Pregnancy and breastfeeding. Claims guide §4.G: state their advice about fish, never our
    conclusion about our fish for that group. The FDA/EPA sentence and the Food Code line are
    verbatim green. The PDF's fertility and preconception copy is held for Clark.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign img_preg = images['omegamaxxing-09-smoked-salmon-toast.jpg'] -%}
  <section class="om-band om-tone--sage" id="om-pregnancy">
    <div class="page-width om-split" style="align-items: center;">
      <div class="om-stack">
        <div class="om-head" data-om-animate>
          <p class="{{ kicker_class }} om-label">If you’re pregnant or breastfeeding</p>
          <h2 class="heading title-lg tracking-heading leading-tight">What FDA and EPA recommend</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="heading title-sm leading-tight">FDA and EPA recommend 2 to 3 servings a week, 4 oz each, from their “Best Choices” list for people who are pregnant or breastfeeding. Salmon is on that list.</p>
        <p class="text-base"><a class="link font-medium" href="https://www.fda.gov/food/consumers/advice-about-eating-fish" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the FDA/EPA advice about eating fish</a></p>
        <h3 class="heading title-sm leading-tight" style="margin-block-start: var(--sp-4);">Raw and smoked fish</h3>
        <p class="text-lg leading-normal">Farmed fish are exempt from the FDA Food Code’s parasite-freezing rule. We blast-freeze at harvest anyway.</p>
        <p class="text-lg leading-normal">Freezing doesn’t eliminate Listeria, though, so standard pregnancy guidance still recommends cooking fish to 145°F and avoiding cold-smoked fish.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="om-media om-media--land">
        {%- if img_preg != blank -%}{{ img_preg | image_url: width: 1800 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 45vw, 100vw', widths: '500,800,1200,1800', alt: 'Smoked salmon on toast with avocado, chives and edible flowers.' }}{%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {%- comment -%} ============================ 08 RECIPE IDEAS ============================ {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- capture om_groups -%}raw|Raw: the most omega-3s|Easy ways to work salmon or steelhead into your week, grouped from most omega-3s kept to least. Every idea works with either fish.|No heat means nothing lost to cooking. Pair with avocado, sesame, olive oil or seaweed so the fat helps you absorb it.|omegamaxxing-19-shiso-roe-bite.jpg|Salmon and roe on a shiso leaf.^liquid|Gently cooked in liquid: most omega-3s kept|Low heat and liquid keep oxygen out, so these are the best cooked options.||omegamaxxing-17-sashimi-chopsticks-overhead.jpg|Sliced salmon and chopsticks on a plate, from above.^bake|One-pan bake: easy and still good|||omegamaxxing-20-one-pan-bake.jpg|Salmon fillets, tomatoes, olives and feta on one sheet pan.{%- endcapture -%}
  {%- assign groups = om_groups | split: '^' -%}
  <section class="om-band" id="om-recipes">
    <div class="page-width om-stack" style="gap: calc(var(--sp-8) * 1.5);">
      <div class="om-head" data-om-animate>
        <p class="{{ kicker_class }} om-label">Chapter 8</p>
        <h2 class="heading title-xl tracking-heading leading-none">Recipe ideas</h2>
      </div>

      {%- for grow in groups -%}
        {%- assign g = grow | split: '|' -%}
        {%- assign gimg = images[g[4]] -%}
        <div class="om-stack" style="gap: var(--sp-6);">
          <div class="om-split{% cycle '', ' om-split--flip', '' %}" style="align-items: start;">
            <div class="om-stack">
              <h3 class="heading title-lg tracking-heading leading-tight" data-om-animate>{{ g[1] }}</h3>
              {%- if g[2] != blank -%}<p class="text-lg leading-normal">{{ g[2] }}</p>{%- endif -%}
              {%- if g[3] != blank -%}<p class="text-lg leading-normal om-italic">{{ g[3] }}</p>{%- endif -%}
              <dl class="om-ideas">
                {%- case g[0] -%}
                  {%- when 'raw' -%}
                    <div><dt class="heading title-sm">Crudo</dt><dd><span class="text-base leading-normal">Thin slices with good olive oil, citrus, flaky salt and a few herbs. Ready in five minutes.</span><span class="om-tags"><a href="/products/steelhead-sashimi-loin-12oz">Steelhead loin</a><a href="/products/scallop-meat-16oz">Scallops</a></span></dd></div>
                    <div><dt class="heading title-sm">Poke bowl</dt><dd><span class="text-base leading-normal">Cubes tossed with tamari, sesame oil and scallion, over rice or greens with avocado and cucumber.</span><span class="om-tags"><a href="/products/atlantic-salmon-2x-6oz-portions">Atlantic salmon</a></span></dd></div>
                    <div><dt class="heading title-sm">Sushi or sashimi</dt><dd><span class="text-base leading-normal">Sliced over seasoned rice, or on its own with a little wasabi and pickled ginger.</span><span class="om-tags"><a href="/products/king-salmon">King salmon</a><a href="/products/atlantic-salmon-2x-6oz-portions">Atlantic salmon</a><a href="/products/steelhead-sashimi-loin-12oz">Steelhead loin</a></span></dd></div>
                    <div><dt class="heading title-sm">Hand rolls</dt><dd><span class="text-base leading-normal">Nori, a spoonful of rice, a strip of fish, avocado and cucumber. Set everything out and let everyone roll their own.</span><span class="om-tags"><a href="/products/atlantic-salmon-2x-6oz-portions">Atlantic salmon</a></span></dd></div>
                    <div><dt class="heading title-sm">Cold-smoked lox</dt><dd><span class="text-base leading-normal">Ready to eat as it comes, with no cooking step.</span><span class="om-tags"><a href="/products/seatopia-steelhead-4oz-smoked">Steelhead lox</a></span></dd></div>
                  {%- when 'liquid' -%}
                    <div><dt class="heading title-sm">Poached in miso soup</dt><dd><span class="text-base leading-normal">Bring the broth to a bare simmer, not a boil. Add bite-size pieces with tofu and greens, and turn off the heat once the fish turns opaque. Stir in the miso last.</span></dd></div>
                    <div><dt class="heading title-sm">Chowder</dt><dd><span class="text-base leading-normal">Build the base first (potatoes, leeks, corn, broth or milk). Add chunks of fish in the last few minutes and let them cook through in the hot soup, off the boil.</span></dd></div>
                    <div><dt class="heading title-sm">Any soup or stew</dt><dd><span class="text-base leading-normal">The same rule works everywhere: add the fish last, keep the heat low, and stop cooking as soon as it’s done.</span></dd></div>
                  {%- when 'bake' -%}
                    <div><dt class="heading title-sm">Sheet-pan or parchment bake</dt><dd><span class="text-base leading-normal">Put fish and vegetables (asparagus, cherry tomatoes, fennel, lemon slices) on one pan with olive oil. Bake at 275–325°F until just done. Wrapping each portion in parchment (en papillote) keeps air out and the fish moist.</span></dd></div>
                    <div><dt class="heading title-sm">Smoked fish: a treat, not the staple</dt><dd><span class="text-base leading-normal">Hot-smoked at home: brine, then smoke low and slow until the fish flakes. Smoking takes longer than other methods, so you’ll lose more omega-3s. Enjoy it for flavor and variety, and flake it onto salads, eggs, toast or pasta.</span></dd></div>
                {%- endcase -%}
              </dl>
              {%- if g[0] == 'raw' -%}
                <p class="text-base leading-normal"><strong>Pregnant?</strong> Skip raw and cold-smoked fish (see <a class="link" href="#om-pregnancy">pregnancy and breastfeeding</a>).</p>
                <p class="text-sm leading-normal text-opacity om-italic">Eating raw or undercooked seafood may increase your risk of foodborne illness. The FDA conservatively suggests cooking to an internal temperature of 145°F.</p>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
            <div class="om-split__media om-stack">
              <div class="om-media om-media--land">
                {%- if gimg != blank -%}{{ gimg | image_url: width: 1800 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 45vw, 100vw', widths: '500,800,1200,1800', alt: g[5] }}{%- endif -%}
                {%- if g[0] == 'liquid' -%}
                  <ul class="om-chips om-chips--over" role="list" data-om-fly><li><span class="om-chip">{{ om_check }}a simmer, not a boil</span></li></ul>
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>
              {%- if g[0] == 'raw' -%}
                {%- assign roe_img = images['omegamaxxing-05-salmon-roe-spoon.jpg'] -%}
                <a class="om-card" href="/products/lab-tested-salmon-roe-caviar" style="color: inherit; text-decoration: none; flex-direction: row; align-items: center; gap: var(--sp-5);">
                  <span class="om-media" style="flex: none; width: 6.5rem; aspect-ratio: 1;">{%- if roe_img != blank -%}{{ roe_img | image_url: width: 300 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', widths: '150,300', sizes: '104px', alt: 'A spoonful of salmon roe.' }}{%- endif -%}</span>
                  <span class="flex flex-col gap-1">
                    <span class="{{ kicker_class }} om-label">Finish anything with roe</span>
                    <span class="text-base leading-normal om-italic">A spoonful of salmon roe adds omega-3s to eggs, salads, potatoes, toast or crudités.</span>
                    <span class="text-sm font-medium" style="text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: .2em;">Shop Salmon Roe Caviar</span>
                  </span>
                </a>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>
          </div>

          {%- liquid
            assign group_blocks = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'recipe'
            assign shown = 0
          -%}
          <div class="om-recipes">
            {%- for block in group_blocks -%}
              {%- if block.settings.group != g[0] -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- assign art = block.settings.article -%}
              {%- if art == blank -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
              {%- assign shown = shown | plus: 1 -%}
              <a class="om-recipe" href="{{ art.url }}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }} data-om-animate data-om-delay="{{ shown | minus: 1 | times: 80 }}">
                <span class="om-media">
                  {%- if art.image != blank -%}{{ art.image | image_url: width: 800 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', sizes: '(min-width: 990px) 22vw, 70vw', widths: '400,600,800', alt: art.image.alt | default: art.title }}{%- endif -%}
                </span>
                <span class="text-sm text-opacity">Recipe</span>
                <span class="om-recipe__title heading title-sm leading-tight">{{ art.title | remove: 'Seafood 101: ' | remove: 'Seafood 201: ' | remove: 'Seafood 101:  ' | strip }}</span>
              </a>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>
        </div>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  </section>

